  "generated_text": "First, we need to find the magnitudes of the complex numbers \\(3-2i\\) and \\(3+2i\\).\n\nThe magnitude of a complex number \\(a + bi\\) is given by:\n\\[\n|a + bi| = \\sqrt{a^2 + b^2}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(3-2i\\):\n\\[\n|3-2i| = \\sqrt{3^2 + (-2)^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 4} = \\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nFor \\(3+2i\\):\n\\[\n|3+2i| = \\sqrt{3^2 + 2^2} = \\sqrt{9 + 4} = \\sqrt{13}\n\\]\n\nNow, we multiply these magnitudes:\n\\[\n|3-2i| \\cdot |3+2i| = \\sqrt{13} \\cdot \\sqrt{13} = (\\sqrt{13} = 13\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(|3-2i| \\cdot |3+2i|\\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{13}\n\\]",
